intertwine|twist-together|VERB|twist together|To twist together, or cause things to twist around one another.|đan vào nhau; quấn vào nhau|The bean stems intertwined around the wooden support.|Những thân cây đậu quấn vào nhau quanh giá đỡ bằng gỗ.|Transitive or intransitive; intertwine something with something; be intertwined. Also used figuratively for connected lives or issues.|-
ruins|remains-of-buildings|NOUN|remains of damaged buildings|The remaining parts of buildings that have been destroyed or have fallen into disrepair.|tàn tích; phế tích|The path led to the ruins of a small stone tower.|Lối mòn dẫn đến tàn tích của một tháp đá nhỏ.|Plural noun: the ruins of a building; the ruins are visible. Distinguish from uncountable ruin meaning destruction.|-
sideways|towards-one-side|ADVERB|towards one side|Towards a side rather than straight forwards or backwards.|sang một bên; theo chiều ngang|Move the cupboard sideways to clear the doorway.|Dịch chiếc tủ sang một bên để thông lối cửa.|Move or step sideways; also sidewise in some usage. Sideways is not the same direction as backwards.|-
whilst|during-the-time|CONJUNCTION|during the time that|During the time that another action or situation is happening.|trong khi|Whilst the soup simmered, I prepared the salad.|Trong khi súp sôi liu riu, tôi chuẩn bị món rau trộn.|Whilst introduces a clause; mainly British English and often more formal than while.|0
whilst|although|CONJUNCTION|although|Used to introduce a fact that contrasts with the main statement.|mặc dù; tuy|Whilst the design is simple, it is difficult to build accurately.|Mặc dù thiết kế đơn giản, việc dựng nó cho chính xác lại khó.|Contrastive whilst is close to although; context distinguishes it from simultaneous-time whilst.|1
district|defined-local-area|NOUN|defined local area|An area of a town or country with a particular boundary or character.|quận; huyện; khu vực|The guide showed us the old market district near the river.|Người hướng dẫn đưa chúng tôi đến khu chợ cũ gần sông.|Countable; a shopping district or an administrative district. Vietnamese quận/huyện depends on the actual administrative system.|0
